// the 128-bit reduced fraction into a double-double `r`.  That ceiling mis-rounds
// the corpus's hardest near-ties (≈58-bit, needing ≈2⁻¹¹¹).  The `Dint` path
// feeds the reduced fraction's bits straight into a 128-bit significand (no dd
